$DATUM (1E,3S)-3-[2-(tert-Butyldiphenylsilyloxy)ethyl]-1-iodo-3,7-dimethylocta-1,6-diene
(9). The following reaction was carried out under Ar. To a cooled (0 °C)
stirred solution of CrCl2 (95%, 282 mg, 2.18 mmol) in THF (0.4 mL) was
added a solution of 18 (70.9 mg, 0.168 mmol) and CHI3 (98%, 273 mg, 0.680
mmol) in 1,4-dioxane (0.8 mL). After being stirred at room temperature
for 3 h, the mixture was quenched with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (10 mL),
diluted with H2O (20 mL), and extracted with CH2Cl2 (15 mL × 5). The
combined extracts were washed with saturated brine (20 mL), dried and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel (EtOAc/hexane, 1:200). 58.7 mg (63%) of 9
and 8.5 mg (12%) of recovered 18. Compound 9 was obtained as a colorless
oil. TLC Rf 0.80 (EtOAc/hexane, 1:6); [α]26 D +5.8 (c 0.645, CHCl3); IR
(neat) 2930 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.93 (s, 3H), 1.04 (s, 9H),
1.21-1.28 (m, 2H), 1.55 (br s, 3H), 1.66 (br s, 3H), 1.52-1.68 (m, 2H),
1.75-1.87 (m, 2H), 3.63 (td, 1H, J = 7.0, 10.3 Hz), 3.66 (td, 1H, J =
7.2, 10.3 Hz), 5.01 (br t, 1H, J = 7.0 Hz), 5.82 (d, 1H, J = 14.6 Hz),
6.37 (d, 1H, J = 14.6 Hz), 7.34-7.46 (m, 6H), 7.62-7.68 (m, 4H); 13C NMR
(125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 17.6, 19.1, 22.58, 22.63, 25.7, 26.9 (3C), 40.9, 42.5,
42.9, 60.6, 73.3, 124.3, 127.7 (4C), 129.6 (2C), 131.5, 133.76, 133.78,
135.6 (4C), 154.3; HRMS (ESI) calcd for C28H40IOSi (M+H+) m/z 547.1893,
found 547.1885.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Total Synthesis of (+)-Vibsanin A
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Takao, Ken-ichi; Tsunoda, Kohei; Kurisu, Takuya; Sakama, Akihiro;
Nishimura, Yoshiyasu; Yoshida, Keisuke; Tadano, Kin-ichi
