$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a stirred solution of
2-(2-((2-(iodoethynyl)phenyl)ethynyl)phenyl)acetaldehyde (8) in THF was
added CrCl2 and NiCl2 at room temperature under argon. After being
stirred at the same temperature for 10 min, the reaction mixture was
poured into H2O. The aqueous layer was extracted with two portions of
diethyl ether. The combined extract was washed with brine, dried over
MgSO4 and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was used for the next
reaction without further purification. Treatment of the precursor 8 with
9.0 equivalents of CrCl2 and 0.64 equivalents of NiCl2 provided the
ten-membered-ring 1,2-dialkynylbenzene derivative 7. Ten-membered-ring
1,2-dialkynylbenzene derivative 7..
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Nozaki-Hiyama-Kishi cyclization
