$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of Aplyronine A-Mycalolide B Hybrid Compound 3. Alcohols 10a
and 10b (preparation of a CH3CN solution of CrCl2-ligand 9 complex) CH3CN
was degassed by freeze-thawing. To a stirred solution of ligand 9 (126
mg, 0.326 mmol) in CH3CN (2.2 mL) were added CrCl2 (40.1 mg, 0.326 mmol)
and proton-sponge® (69.9 mg, 0.326 mmol) at room temperature in a glove
box. The mixture was stirred at room temperature for 2 h in a glove box
to give a CH3CN solution of CrCl2-ligand 9 complex. The solution of the
above-mentioned CrCl2-ligand 9 complex was added to a mixture of the
C21-C28 segment 7 (35.4 mg, 0.0652 mmol), the C29-C34 segment 8 (14.5 mg,
0.0326 mmol), and NiCl2 (dppp) (2.3 M solution in CH3CN, 0.14 mL, 0.32
μmol) at room temperature in a glove box. After being stirred at room
temperature for 3 h in a glove box, the mixture was filtered through a
pad of florisil, and the residue was washed with hexane-EtOAc (1:1). The
filtrate and the washings were combined and concentrated in vacuo. The
crude product was purified by column chromatography on silica gel (5.0 g,
hexane-EtOAc 19:1). Compound: alcohols 10a, Yield: 24.8 mg, 88% and 10b,
Yield: 1.5 mg, 5% as colorless oils, respectively. : 10a:[α]27D -14.9 (c
0.98, CHCl3); IR (CHCl3) 3509, 3033, 2930, 1712, 1597, 1491, 1462, 1256,
1090, 837 cm-1; 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.46-7.41 (m, 6H), 7.32-7.27
(m, 6H), 7.25-7.21 (m, 3H), 5.73 (ddd, J= 15.7, 7.0, 1.3 Hz, 1H), 5.45
(dd, J= 15.7, 4.9 Hz, 1H), 4.82 (dd, J= 10.1, 2.6 Hz, 1H), 4.07 (br s,
1H), 3.97 (tt, J= 7.9, 4.4 Hz, 1H), 3.73-3.65 (m, 2H), 3.34 (s, 3H), 3.23
(ddd, J= 8.9, 7.0, 4.4 Hz, 1H), 3.18 (dt, J= 8.5, 4.0 Hz, 1H), 3.01 (dt,
J= 6.1, 8.9 Hz, 1H), 2.59 (d, J= 3.7 Hz, 1H), 2.51 (apparent sixtet, J=
7.0 Hz, 1H), 2.08 (s, 3H), 2.06 (m, 1H), 1.86 (m, 1H), 1.81-1.70 (m, 2H),
1.66-1.56 (m, 2H), 1.55 (ddd, J= 14.1, 7.9, 4.0 Hz, 1H), 1.35 (m, 1H),
