$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Alcohol 22a and 22b (preparation of a CH3CN solution of CrCl2-ligand 27
complex) CH3CN was degassed by freeze-thawing. To a stirred solution of
ligand 27 (32.9 mg, 0.0754 mmol) in CH3CN (0.50 mL) were added CrCl2 (9.3
mg, 0.076 mmol) and proton-sponge® (16.1 mg, 0.0751 mmol) at room
temperature in a glove box. The mixture was stirred at room temperature
for 2 h in a glove box to give a CH3CN solution of CrCl2-ligand 27
complex. The solution of the above-mentioned CrCl2-ligand 27 complex was
added to a mixture of the C5-C13 segment 11 (10.0 mg, 0.0188 mmol), the
C14-C19 segment 12 (13.9 mg, 0.0377 mmol), and NiCl2(dppp) (1.0 mg,
0.0018 mmol) was added at room temperature in a glove box. After being
stirred at room temperature for 1 h in a glove box, the mixture was
filtered through a pad of florisil, and the residue was washed with
hexane-EtOAc (1:1). The filtrate and the washings were combined and
concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel (2.0 g, hexane-EtOAc 19:1) to afford a
mixture of alcohols 22a and 22b (3.7:1, 14.5 mg, quant.) as a colorless
oil.The diastereomeric ratio of this product was estimated from 1H NMR
(600 MHz) analysis. Analytical samples of 22a and 22b were prepared by
flash column chromatography on silica gel (benzene-Et2O 200:1). 22a:
[α]27D +15.4 (c 0.70, CHCl3); IR (film) 3453, 2957, 1719, 1462, 1382,
1255, 1083, 1006, 837 cm-1; 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.39 (t, J = 7.1
Hz, 1H), 4.23 (dt, J = 10.9, 5.5 Hz, 1H), 4.04 (dt, J = 10.9, 7.4 Hz,
1H), 3.96 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 3.74-3.69 (m, 1H), 3.69-3.60 (m, 2H), 3.41
(dd, J = 4.6, 2.8 Hz, 1H), 2.06 (dt, J = 14.1, 7.1 Hz, 1H), 1.85 (dt, J =
14.1, 7.1 Hz, 1H), 1.83-1.76 (m, 1H), 1.70-1.53 (m, 5H), 1.58 (s, 3H),
1.50-1.43 (m, 1H), 1.42-1.32 (m, 3H), 1.30-1.22 (m, 1H), 1.20 (s, 9H),
0.96 (t, J = 7.9 Hz, 9H), 0.91-0.86 (m, 9H), 0.89 (s, 9H), 0.89 (s, 9H),
0.60 (q, J = 7.9 Hz, 6H), 0.05 (s, 6H), 0.04 (s, 3H), 0.04 (s, 3H). A
signal due to one proton (OH) was not observed; 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 178.5, 137.8, 126.1, 78.9, 77.1, 71.5, 61.7, 61.4, 41.2, 39.7, 38.9,
38.7, 35.0, 33.1, 31.0, 30.1, 28.0, 27.3 (3C), 26.1 (3C), 26.0 (3C),
19.7, 18.5, 18.3, 16.0, 11.0, 10.1, 7.0 (3C), 5.2 (3C), -3.4, -4.0, -5.3,
-5.3; HRMS (ESI) m/z 795.5786, calcd for C42H88NaO6Si3 [M+Na]+ 795.5786.
22b: [α]27D +7.0 (c 1.00, CHCl3); IR (film) 3479, 2957, 1719, 1462, 1380,
1256, 1081, 1006, 837 cm-1; 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.40 (t, J = 7.1
Hz, 1H), 4.23 (dt, J = 10.9, 5.4 Hz, 1H), 4.04 (ddd, J = 10.9, 8.3, 6.5
Hz, 1H), 3.97 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 3.73-3.59 (m, 3H), 3.42 (dd, J = 4.3,
2.9 Hz, 1H), 2.02 (dt, J = 14.1, 7.1 Hz, 1H), 1.90 (dt, J = 14.1, 7.1 Hz,
1H), 1.82-1.76 (m, 1H), 1.72-1.52 (m, 6H), 1.60 (s, 3H), 1.48-1.39 (m,
1H), 1.39-1.21 (m, 3H), 1.19 (s, 9H), 0.95 (t, J = 7.9 Hz, 9H), 0.91 (d,
J = 6.8 Hz, 3H), 0.90-0.86 (m, 6H), 0.89 (s, 9H), 0.89 (s, 9H), 0.59 (q,
J = 7.9 Hz, 6H), 0.05 (s, 6H), 0.05 (s, 3H), 0.04 (s, 3H). A signal due
to one proton (OH) was not observed; 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3) δ 178.5,
138.1, 125.0, 78.4, 76.9, 71.6, 61.7, 61.4, S9 41.1, 39.7, 39.0, 38.7,
34.8, 33.3, 31.0, 30.1, 28.1, 27.2 (3C), 26.1 (3C), 26.0 (3C), 19.5,
18.5, 18.3, 16.1, 11.5, 9.9, 7.0 (3C), 5.1 (3C), -3.3, -4.1, -5.3, -5.3;
HRMS (ESI) m/z 795.5794, calcd for C42H88NaO6Si3 [M+Na]+ 795.5786.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, stereoselective, reaction performed in a glove box,
Nozaki-Hiyama-Kishi coupling reaction, key step, optimization study
(optimized on ligand, nickel complex)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Toward the Second Generation Synthesis of Aplyronine A: Stereocontrolled
Assembly of the C1-C19 Segment by Using an Asymmetric Nozaki-Hiyama-Kishi
Coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kobayashi, Kenichi; Fujii, Yusuke; Hayakawa, Ichiro; Kigoshi, Hideo
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2011), 13(5), 900-903

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME351 STEP1
$RXN



