$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of compound 23. To a suspension of Pd(OAc)2 (24 mg, 0.107 mmol,
0.05 equiv) in dry THF (29 mL) at -78 °C were added PPh3 (28 mg, 0.107
mmol, 0.05 equiv) followed by a solution of the mesylate 22 (866 mg, 5.34
mmol, 2.5 equiv) in dry THF (14 mL) and a solution of the aldehyde 21
(739 mg, 2.14 mmol, 1 equiv) in dry THF (11 mL). A solution of Et2Zn
(6.85 mL, 1 M in hexane, 6.85 mmol, 3.2 equiv) was then added over 2 h
using a syringe pump. The resulting solution was allowed to warm to 0 °C,
and stirred at this temperature for 5 h. Upon completion of the reaction,
monitored by TLC, the reaction mixture was poured into a rapidly stirred
mixture of Et2O, saturated aqueous NH4Cl and ice. The Et2O layer was
separated, washed with saturated aqueous NH4Cl, dried over MgSO4,
filtered and concentrated to give a brown oil. Purification of this
residue by flash chromatography (SiO2, petroleum ether/iPr2O:9/1)
afforded product. A second fraction containing a diastereomeric mixture
was also collected. Yield: (579 mg, 65%), single diastereomer, colorless
oil. diastereomeric mixture: Yield: (165 mg, 19%), dr = 63/37. Rf 0.40
(major isomer) and 0.33 (minor isomer) (cyclohexane/EtOAc:9/1,
Kagi-Mosher). [α]20D +18.3 (c 1.45, CHCl3). 1H NMR (major isomer) (C6D6
300 MHz) δ 5.14 (d, J = 9.1 Hz, 1H), 4.07 (dd, J = 9.1, 6.5 Hz, 1H), 3.96
(d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 3.74 (dd, J = 6.6, 4.8 Hz, 1H), 2.87 (bs, 1H), 2.87
- 2.71 (m, 1H), 1.88 - 1.82 (m, 1H), 1.48 (d, J = 2.4 Hz, 3H), 1.43 (s,
9H), 1.30 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 3H), 1.04 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H), 0.97 - 0.95 (m,
12H), 0.21 (s, 3H), 0.08 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (major isomer) (C6D6 75 MHz) δ
155.8, 81.2, 79.2, 78.9, 78.4, 72.9, 52.6, 31.5, 28.5, 26.4, 20.0, 18.7
(2C), 17.9, 17.6, 3.3, -3.9 (2C). HRMS (ESI/[M+Na]+) calcd. for
C22H43O4NSiNa: 436.2859, found 436.2853.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
