$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Mixture of
(2S,3R,4S)-1,2-(Isopropylidenedioxy)-4,8-dimethyl-4-vinylnon-7-en-3-ol
(14a) and (2S,3R,4R)-isomer (14b). To a stirred solution of 12 (405 mg,
3.11 mmol) in 25 wt% aqueous NH4Cl (8 mL) was added zinc powder (85%,
1.62 g, 21.1 mmol). The mixture was cooled to -5 °C and a solution of 11
(362 mg, 2.09 mmol) in THF (4 mL) was added. After being stirred at -5 °C
for 42 h, the mixture was filtered through a pad of Celite and washed
with EtOAc (10 mL). The combined filtrate and washings were washed with
saturated brine (10 mL), dried and concentrated under reduced pressure.
The residue was purified by column chromatography on silica gel
(EtOAc/hexane, 1:50). 369 mg (66%) of 14a/14b (d.r. = 6:1) and 22.9 mg
(4%) of (2S,3S,4R)-isomer/(2S,3S,4S)-isomer (d.r. = 3:1). Compound
14a/14b (d.r. = 6:1) was obtained as a colorless oil. TLC Rf 0.39
(EtOAc/hexane, 1:6); IR (neat) 3490, 2985, 2915 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) for 14a δ 0.99 (s, 3H), 1.34 (s, 3H), 1.41 (s, 3H), 1.45-1.50 (m,
2H), 1.58 (br s, 3H), 1.67 (br s, 3H), 1.86-1.95 (m, 2H), 2.01 (br, 1H,
OH), 3.75 (dd, 1H, J = 2.5, 2.9 Hz), 3.86-3.91 (m, 2H), 4.15 (ddd, 1H, J
= 2.9, 6.9, 7.5 Hz), 5.03 (dd, 1H, J = 1.2, 17.5 Hz), 5.09 (br t, 1H, J =
7.0 Hz), 5.14 (dd, 1H, J = 1.2, 10.8 Hz), 5.78 (dd, 1H, J = 10.8, 17.5
Hz); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) for 14a δ 17.7, 18.1, 22.5, 25.3, 25.6,
26.4, 37.9, 42.9, 64.3, 76.4, 76.7, 107.4, 114.2, 124.6, 131.3, 143.0;
HRMS (ESI) calcd for C16H28KO3 (M+K+) m/z 307.1676, found 307.1679.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Barbier allylation, other products also detected
